# Phaser Scene Structure Standards

## Description

Establishes consistent patterns for organizing Phaser scenes to enable rapid prototyping while maintaining code quality and reusability.

## Rule

1. Scene File Organization:
   - Each scene MUST be in its own file under `src/scenes/`
   - Scene classes MUST extend `Phaser.Scene`
   - Scene keys MUST be defined as static readonly properties
   - File names MUST match scene keys in kebab-case

2. Scene Lifecycle Methods:
   - MUST implement required lifecycle methods in order:

     ```typescript
     init(): void      // For dynamic initialization
     preload(): void   // For asset loading
     create(): void    // For scene setup
     update(): void    // For game loop logic
     ```

   - MUST use type annotations for all methods and properties
   - MUST clean up all event listeners in shutdown/destroy

3. Asset Management:
   - MUST declare asset keys as static readonly properties
   - MUST use asset manifest for preloading:

     ```typescript
     private static readonly ASSETS = {
       sprites: {
         key: 'path',
         // ...
       },
       audio: {
         key: 'path',
         // ...
       }
     } as const;
     ```

4. Scene Properties:
   - MUST declare class properties at top of file
   - MUST use private/protected for internal properties
   - MUST initialize properties in create() or init()

5. Rapid Prototyping Support:
   - MAY use DEBUG flag for development features
   - MAY include FPS display in debug mode
   - MAY add scene restart hotkey in debug mode

## Implementation

The Cursor IDE will:

- Validate scene file structure
- Check for required lifecycle methods
- Ensure proper type annotations
- Verify asset management patterns
- Flag missing cleanup in shutdown/destroy

## Benefits

- Consistent scene organization
- Reduced boilerplate code
- Easier scene debugging
- Improved asset management
- Better memory management
- Faster prototyping
- Simplified scene transitions

## Examples

✅ Correct:

```typescript
export class GameScene extends Phaser.Scene {
  private static readonly KEY = 'game-scene';
  private static readonly ASSETS = {
    sprites: {
      player: 'assets/player.png'
    }
  } as const;

  private player?: Phaser.GameObjects.Sprite;

  constructor() {
    super({ key: GameScene.KEY });
  }

  preload(): void {
    Object.entries(GameScene.ASSETS.sprites).forEach(([key, path]) => {
      this.load.image(key, path);
    });
  }

  create(): void {
    this.player = this.add.sprite(400, 300, 'player');
    
    if (process.env.DEBUG) {
      this.add.fps();
      this.input.keyboard.on('keydown-R', () => this.scene.restart());
    }
  }

  update(): void {
    // Game loop logic
  }

  shutdown(): void {
    this.input.keyboard.off('keydown-R');
    this.player?.destroy();
  }
}
```

❌ Incorrect:

```typescript
class GameScene extends Phaser.Scene {
  player;
  
  preload() {
    this.load.image('player', 'player.png');
  }
  
  create() {
    this.player = this.add.sprite(400, 300, 'player');
  }
}
```
